The matrix is

\[
A=\begin{pmatrix}5&-4\\0&1\end{pmatrix}.
\]

Its determinant is

\[
\det(A)=5(1)-(-4)(0)=5\neq 0,
\]

so the inverse exists. For a \(2\times 2\) matrix,

\[
\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\c&d\end{pmatrix}^{-1}
=
\frac{1}{ad-bc}
\begin{pmatrix}d&-b\\-c&a\end{pmatrix}.
\]

Thus,

\[
A^{-1}
=
\frac{1}{5}
\begin{pmatrix}1&4\\0&5\end{pmatrix}
=
\boxed{
\begin{pmatrix}
\frac15 & \frac45\\
0 & 1
\end{pmatrix}
}.
\]

